{"run_id": "47fba9dc564b", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0009", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "**Step‑by‑step solution**\n\n1. **First week:**  \n   Recorded cases = 5,000.\n\n2. **Second week:**  \n   “Half as many … as the first week” → \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5{,}000 = 2{,}500 \\) cases.\n\n3. **Third week:**  \n   “2000 more cases were recorded” → 2,000 more than the second week:  \n   \\( 2{,}500 + 2{,}000 = 4{,}500 \\) cases.\n\n4. **Total after three weeks:**  \n   \\[\n   5{,}000 + 2{,}500 + 4{,}500 = 12{,}000\n   \\]\n\n**Final answer:** 12000.  \nFinal answer: 12000", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:16:38.137229+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 173, "completion_tokens": 286, "total_tokens": 459, "reasoning_tokens": 94}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 23.64, "tier2_label": "incorrect", "tier2_extracted": 12000.0, "original_correct": 0}
{"run_id": "d400410cda2f", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0014", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "**Step 1: Determine weekday reading time**  \n- Newspaper: 30 minutes each weekday.  \n- Novel: 1 hour = 60 minutes each weekday.  \n- Total per weekday = 30 min + 60 min = **90 minutes**.  \n\n**Step 2: Compute total for the 5 weekdays**  \n\\(5 \\text{ days} \\times 90 \\text{ minutes/day} = 450 \\text{ minutes}\\).\n\n**Step 3: Determine weekend reading time**  \nHe “doubles his reading time” on Saturday and Sunday, so each weekend day he reads twice the weekday total:  \n\\(2 \\times 90 \\text{ minutes} = 180 \\text{ minutes}\\) per weekend day.\n\n**Step 4: Compute total for the 2 weekend days**  \n\\(2 \\text{ days} \\times 180 \\text{ minutes/day} = 360 \\text{ minutes}\\).\n\n**Step 5: Add weekday and weekend totals**  \n\\(450 \\text{ minutes} + 360 \\text{ minutes} = 810 \\text{ minutes}\\).\n\n**Final answer:**  \nFinal answer: 810", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:17:05.863803+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 164, "completion_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 523, "reasoning_tokens": 103}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 27.72, "tier2_label": "correct", "tier2_extracted": 810.0, "original_correct": 1}
{"run_id": "ba0fdf666828", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0032", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "Helen washes her pillowcases once every 4 weeks.  \nThere are 52 weeks in a year, so the number of washings in a year is  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{52\\text{ weeks}}{4\\text{ weeks per wash}} = 13 \\text{ washings}.\n\\]\n\nEach washing takes 30 minutes, so the total time spent washing in a year is  \n\n\\[\n13 \\times 30\\text{ minutes} = 390\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\nThus, Helen spends **390 minutes** (which is 6 hours 30 minutes) hand washing her pillowcases each year.  \n\nFinal answer: 390.", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:17:29.568049+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 145, "completion_tokens": 231, "total_tokens": 376, "reasoning_tokens": 84}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 23.7, "tier2_label": "correct", "tier2_extracted": 390.0, "original_correct": 1}
{"run_id": "a8034b2fb513", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0061", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "First, assume the most Martin is willing to spend is \\$1,000.  \n\n1. The clerk first reduces the price by \\$100:  \n\\[\n\\$1,000 - \\$100 = \\$900.\n\\]\n\n2. Then the clerk applies an additional 20 % discount to the \\$900 price:  \n\\[\n20\\% \\text{ of } \\$900 = 0.20 \\times 900 = \\$180.\n\\]  \nSubtract this discount:  \n\\[\n\\$900 - \\$180 = \\$720.\n\\]\n\n3. The amount Martin originally planned to spend was \\$1,000, and the final price is \\$720.  \nThe difference (how much lower the price is) is:  \n\\[\n\\$1,000 - \\$720 = \\$280.\n\\]\n\n**Final answer: 280**", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:17:53.088826+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 161, "completion_tokens": 286, "total_tokens": 447, "reasoning_tokens": 107}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 23.52, "tier2_label": "correct", "tier2_extracted": 280.0, "original_correct": 1}
{"run_id": "b8f42f31cdc7", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0072", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "Let  \n\n- \\(d\\) be the depth from the seabed to the base of the hill.  \n- \\(H\\) be the vertical distance from the riverbed (seabed) to the peak of the hill.  \n\nWe are told:\n\n1. The base of the hill is \\(300\\text{ m}\\) above the seabed, so \\(d = 300\\text{ m}\\).\n2. This depth \\(d\\) is a quarter of the total vertical distance to the peak:  \n\n\\[\nd = \\frac{1}{4}H \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad H = 4d.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(d = 300\\text{ m}\\):\n\n\\[\nH = 4 \\times 300\\text{ m} = 1200\\text{ m}.\n\\]\n\nThe height of the hill itself is the difference between the peak elevation and the base elevation:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Hill height} = H - d = 1200\\text{ m} - 300\\text{ m} = 900\\text{ m}.\n\\]\n\n**Final answer: 900**.", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:18:21.657311+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 146, "completion_tokens": 370, "total_tokens": 516, "reasoning_tokens": 123}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 28.56, "tier2_label": "correct", "tier2_extracted": 900.0, "original_correct": 1}
{"run_id": "d0601f9590b3", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0077", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "The ages form a geometric sequence where each term is 1.5 times the previous one:\n\n- \\(a_1 = 4080\\)\n- \\(a_2 = 1.5 \\times 4080\\)\n- \\(a_3 = 1.5^2 \\times 4080\\)\n- \\(a_4 = 1.5^3 \\times 4080\\)\n- \\(a_5 = 1.5^4 \\times 4080\\)\n\nCalculate \\(1.5^4 = 5.0625\\).\n\nThen  \n\\(a_5 = 4080 \\times 5.0625 = 20\\,655\\).\n\n**Final answer: 20655**", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:18:47.996107+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 147, "completion_tokens": 340, "total_tokens": 487, "reasoning_tokens": 180}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 26.34, "tier2_label": "correct", "tier2_extracted": 20655.0, "original_correct": 1}
{"run_id": "2b976f4ddeaa", "status": "ok", "question_id": "math_0111", "category": "math", "provider": "groq", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "sample_id": 0, "response_text": "First, determine the number of episodes in each season:\n\n- Seasons before the announcement: 9 seasons, each with 22 episodes.  \n  \\(9 \\times 22 = 198\\) episodes.\n\n- The announced final season is 4 episodes longer than a typical season:  \n  \\(22 + 4 = 26\\) episodes.\n\nNow add the episodes from all seasons:\n\n\\(198 + 26 = 224\\) episodes total.\n\nEach episode runs for 0.5 hours, so the total viewing time is:\n\n\\(224 \\times 0.5 = 112\\) hours.\n\n**Final answer: 112**", "finish_reason": "stop", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T13:19:11.460042+00:00", "token_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 171, "completion_tokens": 285, "total_tokens": 456, "reasoning_tokens": 145}, "parameters": {"temperature": 0.7, "reasoning_effort": "low"}, "latency_s": 23.46, "tier2_label": "correct", "tier2_extracted": 112.0, "original_correct": 1}
